## 7. Compliance

| ID | Requirement | Testable Criterion |
|----|-------------|-------------------|
| CXC-PRIM-C1 | Composites, not code widgets | Each primitive is a `components:` entry expanded by `expand_components`; no new engine `Widget` subclass is required for the four pure composites |
| CXC-PRIM-C2 | Forkable | A demo `.compose.yaml` uses `{use: <name>, …}`; cloning the component and changing tokens restyles it with no engine change |
| CXC-PRIM-C3 | Shared tokens | All six render in the ratified token set ([CXC-PRIM-TOKENS]); pre-vis is the visual reference |
| CXC-PRIM-C4 | progress_bar | fill width tracks a bound value 0..1; warn threshold flips color via binding, not a new widget |
| CXC-PRIM-C5 | switch | tap toggles a binary namespace; knob position is a bound expression on that state |
| CXC-PRIM-C6 | slider | `on_pan` publishes a normalized value ([CXC-PRIM-DRAGVAL]); thumb tracks the published value; an Intelligence publish moves it identically |
| CXC-PRIM-C7 | dropdown | item selection publishes + dismisses via the popup overlay ([CXC-PRIM-POPUP]); outside tap dismisses without change |
| CXC-PRIM-C8 | numpad / keyboard | key presses edit a target text namespace a `text_input` consumes |
| CXC-PRIM-C9 | Backends | Each composite renders via the Canvas contract with no per-backend widget code (define-once) |
| CXC-PRIM-C10 | repeat generator | `repeat: N as: i` unrolls a child into N concrete children with `{{i}}` = 0..N−1 at load; composes with `{{param}}` and `use:`; no new per-backend code |
| CXC-PRIM-C11 | segment_bar | An N-segment bar lights `floor`/threshold segments by a bound value, zoned green/yellow/red by count params, in horizontal or vertical orientation; all per-segment logic is one DSL expression |
| CXC-PRIM-C12 | fill/fader ([CXC-PRIM-FADER]) | `gauge` `style: bar` fills a track by a `namespace:`-bound value's fraction of `[min_val,max_val]`; `orientation: vertical` fills bottom->top, `horizontal` left->right; the fill warms on `warning_threshold`/`danger_threshold`; the dial/semicircle rendering is byte-unchanged (a new style branch only) |
| CXC-PRIM-C13 | led_bar readout ([CXC-PRIM-LEDBAR]) | `gauge` `style: led_bar` lights segment i when `value >= min_val+(i/N)*range`; an unlit segment is a 16%-luminance hue-true SAME-color; a short `segment_colors` repeats its last entry; `orientation`+`reverse` place the axis+origin (and fully express the module H/V flip, no third knob). Defaults (rectangular, `across`, gap 4, padding 8, `min_segment_size` 0) render byte-identical to the pre-enhancement output; dial/semicircle/bar branches unchanged |
| CXC-PRIM-C14 | led_bar config params ([CXC-PRIM-LEDBAR]) | `segment_shape` ∈ {rectangular,square,round} draws the specified geometry; `segment_long_axis` ∈ {across,along} flips the rectangular long axis (rectangular only); `segment_gap`/`padding` measurably change spacing/inset; `min_segment_size` clamps the short-axis extent, recovering by gap-shrink then count-rescale — never rendering below the floor nor overflowing the rect |
| CXC-PRIM-C15 | tier parity ([CXC-PRIM-TIER-PARITY]) | each new UX capability renders on Python/Skia AND the C++ embedded back-end over the one Canvas contract, OR carries an explicit `console-only:` scope + reason; a Skia-only capability is Draft, not landed. `led_bar`/`bar` are contract-clean (`fill_round_rect`/`fill_circle`/`draw_line` only), so their embedded port is a back-end pass |
| CXC-PRIM-C16 | carousel geometry ([CXC-PRIM-CAROUSEL], [CXC-PRIM-CAROUSEL-MODEL]) | a headless render at `position ∈ {0.0,0.5,1.0,2.0}` yields each tile's `x=W/2+(i−position)*S` and clamped `scale=max(side,center−(center−side)*min(1,\|i−position\|))`; center tile lifted; off-screen tiles culled without changing on-screen x/scale ([CXC-PRIM-CAROUSEL-VERIFY] CAR-V1) |
| CXC-PRIM-C17 | carousel touch model ([CXC-PRIM-CAROUSEL-TOUCH]) | drag moves `position` 1:1 (`S` px = 1 pane); release is a TAP iff drift<`tap_max_drift_px` and duration<`tap_max_duration_ms`; a swipe advances EXACTLY ±1 iff `\|dx\|>snap_threshold*S` OR `\|v\|>flick_velocity`, else snaps back; NO multi-tile momentum; snap eases `1−(1−t)³` over `snap_duration_ms`; edge overshoot ×`elastic_factor`; a drag cancels an in-flight snap ([CXC-PRIM-CAROUSEL-VERIFY] CAR-V3/V4/V5/V7) |
| CXC-PRIM-C18 | uniform tile scale, image + live ([CXC-PRIM-CAROUSEL-SCALE], [CXC-PRIM-CAROUSEL-TILES]) | an image tile and a live-widget (`fiat_widget`/`bsg_app`) tile draw at the SAME `scale_i` for the same distance via ONE canvas scale transform (no `SCALE_STEPS` pre-render cache); mixing kinds shows no scale seam ([CXC-PRIM-CAROUSEL-VERIFY] CAR-V8) |
| CXC-PRIM-C19 | carousel bindings / control-is-a-peer ([CXC-PRIM-CAROUSEL-BIND]) | the centered index/id publishes to `index_ns` on settle; publishing an index to `goto_ns` snaps identically to a swipe; a center-tap publishes the tile's `_app/<target>/open` (launch-bar convention, [CXC-LB-INTENT-BINDING]) or `activate_ns`, and nothing else ([CXC-PRIM-CAROUSEL-VERIFY] CAR-V2/V6) |
| CXC-PRIM-C20 | carousel tier waiver ([CXC-PRIM-CAROUSEL-TIER]) | the carousel carries an explicit console/desktop-tier WAIVER + reason and an UPHOLDS edge to [CXC-PRIM-TIER-PARITY]; the embedded case is a distinct reduced variant, not a claimed port ([CXC-PRIM-CAROUSEL-VERIFY] CAR-V9) |

